            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to take a dip, then the Bengali for to splash."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ভ্রমণ করা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভ্রমণ করা — bhrômôn kôrā — \"to travel; to tour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গত বছর আমরা পাহাড়ে ভ্রমণ করলাম। gôtô bôchhôr āmrā pāhāṛe bhrômôn kôrlām. Last year we travelled in the hills."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি অনেক দেশ ভ্রমণ করলেন, tini ônek desh bhrômôn kôrlen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A careful word, for travel writing and the news; বেড়ানো is the everyday one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভ্রমণ করা (bhrômôn kôrā) joins Sanskrit bhramaṇa, \"wandering, roaming about\" (Monier-Williams), to করা, to do."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
